1
00:00:04,993 --> 00:00:07,251
Whiskers and the Singing Glass.

2
00:00:16,982 --> 00:00:19,712
Luna loved her little golden bell.

3
00:00:28,082 --> 00:00:30,437
Oof. There's something under my bottom.

4
00:00:34,722 --> 00:00:36,480
Whiskers! Have you seen my bell?

5
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:39,507
Your bell? Um... it was like that already.

6
00:00:39,707 --> 00:00:42,116
It's squashed flat. It doesn't ring anymore.

7
00:00:42,316 --> 00:00:45,480
Probably a mouse did it. A big, heavy mouse.

8
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,065
Hey! I heard that!

9
00:00:50,442 --> 00:00:54,433
Grandma brought it from Venice. She said the glass there sings like a bell.

10
00:00:54,633 --> 00:00:57,058
Then we go to Venice. Right now.

11
00:00:57,258 --> 00:00:59,827
You? Whiskers, you never want to go anywhere!

12
00:01:00,027 --> 00:01:02,182
I... suddenly love travelling.

13
00:01:06,013 --> 00:01:08,677
Look! The mail plane to Venice! Bring me a present!

14
00:01:20,678 --> 00:01:26,475
So two cats hid among the letters in the little mail plane, and flew over the mountains.

15
00:01:33,029 --> 00:01:35,116
Don't look down. Don't look down.

16
00:01:35,316 --> 00:01:37,208
Whiskers, look down! There it is!

17
00:01:44,670 --> 00:01:47,333
Wait. The whole city is sitting in the water?

18
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:51,025
Venice has canals for streets, and boats for buses.

19
00:02:02,119 --> 00:02:07,463
They landed by Saint Mark's Square, with its golden church and tall bell tower.

20
00:02:07,663 --> 00:02:10,055
Lots and lots of pigeons.

21
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:12,862
We fly home when the big bell rings at sunset!

22
00:02:16,693 --> 00:02:18,373
Sniff, sniff. A doughnut?

23
00:02:18,573 --> 00:02:23,179
A sugary doughnut rolled to his paws. But the pigeons saw it too.

24
00:02:23,379 --> 00:02:25,488
Shoo! This doughnut is for cats!

25
00:02:43,843 --> 00:02:45,704
Blub! Not the water again!

26
00:02:49,989 --> 00:02:52,279
Ha! I have caught a fish with whiskers!

27
00:02:52,479 --> 00:02:55,047
I meant to do that. I needed a bath.

28
00:02:55,247 --> 00:02:57,823
I am Bepi, the singing gondolier. Hop in!

29
00:02:58,023 --> 00:02:59,817
We're looking for glass that sings!

30
00:03:00,017 --> 00:03:02,778
Then to Murano, to Nonna Vetra! Andiamo!

31
00:03:08,425 --> 00:03:10,602
La la laaa! The Rialto Bridge!

32
00:03:17,156 --> 00:03:18,816
Whiskers, you're very quiet.

33
00:03:19,016 --> 00:03:21,144
Just thinking. About... bells.

34
00:03:21,344 --> 00:03:22,542
Sing with me!

35
00:03:22,742 --> 00:03:24,114
Meeeow la laaa!

36
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:37,406
Murano: the island of glassmakers.

37
00:03:37,606 --> 00:03:40,218
Welcome! What can Nonna Vetra make for you?

38
00:03:40,418 --> 00:03:42,787
A new bell, please. Mine got squashed.

39
00:03:42,987 --> 00:03:44,373
Squashed? How?

40
00:03:49,112 --> 00:03:51,846
It was me. I rolled on it in my sleep.

41
00:03:52,046 --> 00:03:55,492
Not on purpose. I'm sorry I didn't tell you, Luna.

42
00:03:55,692 --> 00:03:58,592
Oh, Whiskers. So that's why you came all this way.

43
00:03:58,792 --> 00:04:00,502
Thank you for telling me the truth.

44
00:04:00,702 --> 00:04:03,312
A brave sorry! Now, help me blow the glass.

45
00:04:09,866 --> 00:04:12,021
Gently! It's a bell, not a balloon!

46
00:04:18,576 --> 00:04:21,232
A bell made with a friend sings the sweetest.

47
00:04:25,063 --> 00:04:26,407
Listen! It sings!

48
00:04:26,607 --> 00:04:28,886
The sunset bell! Quick, to the gondola!

49
00:04:34,532 --> 00:04:38,804
But the tide had come in. Acqua alta! The square was flooded.

50
00:04:42,635 --> 00:04:44,484
The square is a swimming pool!

51
00:04:44,684 --> 00:04:47,371
In Venice, where there is water, there is a gondola!

52
00:04:55,741 --> 00:04:56,858
Grazie, Bepi!

53
00:04:57,058 --> 00:04:58,419
Ciao, little cats!

54
00:05:11,328 --> 00:05:14,580
The little plane carried them home through the night.

55
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:21,112
Did you find the singing glass?

56
00:05:21,312 --> 00:05:22,056
Listen.

57
00:05:26,342 --> 00:05:28,687
And for you, Pip: a glass mouse.

58
00:05:28,887 --> 00:05:31,671
Now, a nap. Far away from all bells.

59
00:05:31,871 --> 00:05:38,460
Because saying sorry is the first step to fixing what is broken. And friends help with the rest.

